var o=[{title:`Benches for support and pressing`,text:`A flat bench supports presses, rows and seated movements. An adjustable bench changes your torso angle for presses and other exercises. Check that its stated capacity covers you plus any external weight, lock the adjustment, and make sure it does not rock or slide before you load it. A chair is not automatically a safe weight bench.`},{title:`A stable step`,text:`Step-ups, incline push-ups and low step conditioning need a platform that will not tip. Start with a low step that lets your hip and knee move with control. Place your whole supporting foot on the step, step down deliberately, and do not push off the trailing foot to hide a platform that is too high.`},{title:`Fitting a jump rope`,text:`As a rough first check, stand with one foot on the middle of the rope and lift the handles. Many recreational ropes fit when the handles reach about the lower chest or armpits, although rope design and skill change the ideal length. A rope that is too short hits your feet. One that is too long catches the ground and can lead to big arm circles.`},{title:`Check the space and the gear`,text:`Use a non-slip floor and look out for furniture, lights, fans and other people. Jump rope needs room overhead and to the sides as well as floor space. Before each session, check for worn rope coatings, sharp wire ends, damaged bench hinges and loose step surfaces. Replace broken equipment instead of improvising repairs.`},{title:`Using TrainUp`,text:`Set your bench type, floor size, ceiling height, surface, and whether jumping is OK in Profile, and the plan picks only exercises that fit them. If your knees or space rule out a step, or noise, impact or ceiling height rule out the rope, step-free exercises and stationary marching are the alternatives.`}];var s=[{label:`ACE exercise library`,url:`https://www.acefitness.org/resources/everyone/exercise-library/`},{label:`Mayo Clinic: weight-training safety and technique`,url:`https://www.mayoclinic.org/healthy-lifestyle/fitness/in-depth/weight-training/art-20045842`},{label:`2026 ACSM position stand`,url:`https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41843416/`}];var a={sections:o,sources:s};export{a as default,o as sections,s as sources};